    <bf:title>
      <bf:Title>
	<bf:mainTitle>John : discovering christ's beauty through gospel imagery</bf:mainTitle>
      </bf:Title>
    </bf:title>
    <bf:content>
      <bf:Content rdf:about="http://id.loc.gov/vocabulary/contentTypes/txt">
	<rdfs:label>text</rdfs:label>
	<bf:code>txt</bf:code>
      </bf:Content>
    </bf:content>
    <bf:summary>
      <bf:Summary>
	<rdfs:label>"God's Word nourishes the heart, mind, and spirit. But too often today's busy woman is surviving-barely-on spiritual snacks snatched from the margins of her day. Distractions sidetrack us from what God longs for us to know. This study of the book of John invites women to encounter the Savior through John's unique images of Jesus-as the Word, the Light of the World, the Living Water, the Good Shepherd, and more. In exploring these winsome pictures, Sue Edwards, Emma Reid, and Ali Shaw encourage women to leave behind their presuppositions and personal agendas in order to get to know Jesus more intimately. Perfect for small groups, women's ministries, and individual reflection, this study of John's gospel is accessible to new Christians yet substantial enough for lifelong believers who want to go deeper"-- Provided by publisher.</rdfs:label>
      </bf:Summary>
    </bf:summary>
